 "answer": "# Part A: Tax Calculation\n\n**Tax brackets on $81,900:**\n- 8% on first $11,000 = $880.00\n- 20% on next $34,000 ($11,000\u2013$45,000) = $6,800.00\n- 30% on remaining $36,900 (above $45,000) = $11,070.00\n\nSubtotal tax = 880 + 6,800 + 11,070 = **$18,750.00**\n\n**Tax credit:**\n- Base credit = $1,800\n- Reduction = 5% \u00d7 ($81,900 \u2212 $50,000) = 5% \u00d7 $31,900 = $1,595\n- Adjusted credit = 1,800 \u2212 1,595 = $205 (positive, so keep as is)\n\n**Tax owed** = 18,750 \u2212 205 = **$18,545.00**\n\n# Part B: Chinese Remainder Problem\n\nNeed x \u2261 5 (mod 9), x \u2261 3 (mod 19), x \u2261 4 (mod 16).\n\n**Combine first two:** x = 9k+5 \u2261 3 (mod 19) \u2192 9k \u2261 -2 \u2261 17 (mod 19). \nInverse of 9 mod 19 is 17 (since 9\u00d717=153=8\u00d719+1). \nk \u2261 17\u00d717 = 289 \u2261 4 (mod 19) \u2192 x = 171m + 41.\n\n**Combine with third:** 171m + 41 \u2261 4 (mod 16). \n171 \u2261 11 (mod 16), 41 \u2261 9 (mod 16): 11m + 9 \u2261 4 \u2192 11m \u2261 11 (mod 16). \nSince gcd(11,16)=1 and inverse of 11 mod 16 is 3 (11\u00d73=33\u22611): m \u2261 3\u00d711 = 33 \u2261 1 (mod 16).\n\nSo m = 1 gives smallest solution: x = 171(1) + 41 = **212**\n\nCheck: 212=23\u00d79+5 \u2713; 212=11\u00d719+3 \u2713; 212=13\u00d716+4 \u2713\n\n# Part C: FIFO Cost of Goods Sold\n\n**Track lot consumption through sales (total sold = 547 units):**\n\n- **Sale 1 (120):** 120 from Lot1 \u2192 120\u00d74.15 = 498.00 (Lot1 left: 20)\n- **Sale 2 (95):** 20 from Lot1 + 75 from Lot2 \u2192 20\u00d74.15 + 75\u00d78.73 = 83.00+654.75 = 737.75 (Lot2 left: 8)\n- **Sale 3 (79):** 8 from Lot2 + 71 from Lot3 \u2192 8\u00d78.73+71\u00d710.67 = 69.84+757.57 = 827.41 (Lot3 left: 81)\n- **Sale 4 (78):** 78 from Lot3 \u2192 78\u00d710.67 = 832.26 (Lot3 left: 3)\n- **Sale 5 (58):** 3 from Lot3 + 55 from Lot4 \u2192 3\u00d710.67+55\u00d710.03 = 32.01+551.65 = 583.66 (Lot4 left: 97)\n- **Sale 6 (117):** 97 from Lot4 + 20 from Lot5 \u2192 97\u00d710.03+20\u00d76.00 = 972.91+120.00 =